WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.357
Welcome to R&D Tax Workbench Canada! In this walkthrough, we'll prepare a complete SR&ED

2
00:00:05.357 --> 00:00:10.113
claim for Northvane Sensing, an Ontario company with a lab in Quebec, from sign-up to

3
00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:14.870
the T661, Schedule 31 and the provincial credit forms. Let's dive in!

4
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.680
Getting started takes seconds. Create an account with your name, your email and a password.

5
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.080
Confirm the password, and you're in.

6
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.660
The AI features, like project setup, account classification and the T661 descriptions,

7
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.680
run on credits. Open the credit meter, choose a top-up, and pay securely through Stripe.

8
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.505
The Canadian edition is sold to businesses, so the business name and GST/HST number are

9
00:00:45.505 --> 00:00:48.930
needed once, before your first top-up.

10
00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:57.667
Pay by card through Stripe's secure checkout.

11
00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.752
Add the billing address, and pay.

12
00:01:10.865 --> 00:01:14.705
Payment confirmed, and the credits land in your balance straight away.

13
00:01:21.318 --> 00:01:25.313
Create a new claim. Choose the claimant, a corporation, then its legal name, business

14
00:01:25.313 --> 00:01:29.308
number and status: a Canadian-controlled private corporation.

15
00:01:32.518 --> 00:01:36.468
Then the tax year. It begins after 15 December 2024, so the new federal rules apply: the

16
00:01:36.468 --> 00:01:40.418
$6 million expenditure limit, and capital expenditures qualify. In Quebec, the new CRIC

17
00:01:40.418 --> 00:01:44.368
applies.

18
00:01:44.768 --> 00:01:47.978
Choose the provinces with a permanent establishment, Ontario and Quebec, and the proxy

19
00:01:47.978 --> 00:01:51.188
method. Then create the claim.

20
00:01:55.568 --> 00:01:58.438
Add the address. Every change saves automatically.

21
00:02:06.564 --> 00:02:11.179
Claim settings hold the figures the credits depend on: prior-year taxable capital and

22
00:02:11.179 --> 00:02:15.794
income, for the expenditure limit and the refund rate, and the tax otherwise payable.

23
00:02:16.194 --> 00:02:19.239
The Ontario figures for its innovation tax credit. Only the questions for the company's

24
00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:22.284
own provinces are shown.

25
00:02:29.154 --> 00:02:32.629
Government assistance, like this NRC IRAP contribution, reduces the pool and the qualified

26
00:02:32.629 --> 00:02:36.104
expenditures, so it's recorded here.

27
00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:39.259
Then the T661 contacts and funding sources, and the total overhead that caps the proxy

28
00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:42.014
amount.

29
00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.880
Now the SR&ED project. Paste in your own notes, and the AI project setup drafts the project

30
00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.650
for you.

31
00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.580
It proposes the SR&ED work, and the support work that serves it, in the terms the CRA

32
00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.110
uses.

33
00:03:12.754 --> 00:03:15.549
Create the project, and every description is written in one go: the project overview,

34
00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:18.344
and each activity.

35
00:03:25.743 --> 00:03:29.613
Every activity now has its full description, ready to review and edit.

36
00:03:37.963 --> 00:03:43.343
Then T661, Part 2. Add the dates and the field of science, and AI drafts lines 242, 244

37
00:03:43.343 --> 00:03:48.723
and 246 from your notes and descriptions, within the CRA's word limits.

38
00:04:01.503 --> 00:04:04.353
It adds no facts. Anything it can't find is left as a question for you, so review each

39
00:04:04.353 --> 00:04:07.203
line and make it yours.

40
00:04:11.356 --> 00:04:14.649
Payroll next. Upload the payroll file, and AI maps the columns: salary, bonuses, taxable

41
00:04:14.649 --> 00:04:17.942
benefits, hours worked, and the province of employment. Employer CPP and EI stay out of

42
00:04:17.942 --> 00:04:21.236
salary.

43
00:04:21.636 --> 00:04:26.856
A quick quality check, then import. 8 employees are loaded, with the Quebec staff in Quebec.

44
00:04:27.256 --> 00:04:30.936
The CTO owns a quarter of the shares, so mark her as a specified employee. Her bonus is

45
00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:34.616
left out, and the specified-employee rules apply.

46
00:04:37.389 --> 00:04:40.389
Now the timesheet. The parser reads each person's SR&ED hours, and matches them to the

47
00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:43.389
activities by title.

48
00:04:43.789 --> 00:04:46.589
6 people, each allocated to the right activity.

49
00:04:53.049 --> 00:04:57.804
The combined view brings it together: each person's salary, bonus and benefits, apportioned

50
00:04:57.804 --> 00:05:02.559
by actual SR&ED hours. The two people with no SR&ED hours stay out of the claim.

51
00:05:04.855 --> 00:05:09.345
Now the financials. Upload the general ledger. Every account is read and checked.

52
00:05:09.745 --> 00:05:13.690
20 accounts and 121 transactions. Import them, and AI classifies each one for SR&ED, with

53
00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:17.635
a reason for every decision.

54
00:05:19.655 --> 00:05:22.995
Upload the trial balance separately, and AI classifies it too.

55
00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.310
It spots the new environmental test chamber as capital property bought this year.

56
00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.485
Salaries, contracts and materials are picked out as SR&ED. Rent, cloud and software are

57
00:05:36.485 --> 00:05:40.810
overhead, covered by the proxy amount, and loan interest is excluded.

58
00:05:42.826 --> 00:05:47.236
Then the income statement and the balance sheet, each read and saved to the claim.

59
00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:05.476
The ledger is an expense-only extract, so mark it as partial, and every source reconciles.

60
00:06:10.226 --> 00:06:14.256
Apportionment. Salaries follow the timesheets. Under the proxy method, overhead is covered

61
00:06:14.256 --> 00:06:18.286
by the prescribed proxy amount, so it isn't claimed twice.

62
00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:32.213
Contractors. Choose the T661 line for each one, and where the work was done.

63
00:06:32.613 --> 00:06:36.858
Ottawa Valley Composites built the clamp housings at arm's length, so it goes on line

64
00:06:36.858 --> 00:06:41.103
340, and 80% of it qualifies for the federal credit.

65
00:06:48.713 --> 00:06:51.708
Gatineau Test Labs ran the icing tunnel in Quebec. It's a Quebec subcontract, so half

66
00:06:51.708 --> 00:06:54.703
of it counts for the CRIC.

67
00:07:06.213 --> 00:07:10.433
Link each contractor to the activities it worked on, as evidence for the claim.

68
00:07:27.705 --> 00:07:31.685
Other expenses. AI has already found the materials consumed in testing. Under the proxy

69
00:07:31.685 --> 00:07:35.665
method, overhead isn't claimed: the proxy amount replaces it.

70
00:07:36.065 --> 00:07:39.595
In claim settings, each account goes on its T661 line.

71
00:07:39.995 --> 00:07:44.670
The test chamber from the trial balance is capital property, bought in June 2025 and used

72
00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:49.345
all or substantially all for SR&ED, so it goes on line 390.

73
00:07:51.358 --> 00:07:56.358
The summary. The federal credit is $264,000, with $79,000 refunded after tax, plus $115,000

74
00:07:56.358 --> 00:08:01.358
in provincial credits.

75
00:08:01.758 --> 00:08:06.398
Every T661 and Schedule 31 line is worked out: current and capital expenditures, the proxy

76
00:08:06.398 --> 00:08:11.038
amount, assistance, and the 35% enhanced credit.

77
00:08:11.438 --> 00:08:15.958
Ontario's innovation and R&D tax credits, and Quebec's CRIC, each with its form.

78
00:08:16.918 --> 00:08:19.603
Any point the law can read more than one way is listed as a position for you to decide,

79
00:08:19.603 --> 00:08:22.288
with its source.

80
00:08:25.791 --> 00:08:30.151
Outputs. Drafts of every form the claim needs, with anything still to complete.

81
00:08:30.551 --> 00:08:35.151
The T661, line by line, ready to copy into the return or your tax software.

82
00:08:35.551 --> 00:08:41.891
Schedule 31, the Ontario schedules, and Quebec's RD-1029.8 for the CO-17 return.

83
00:08:42.291 --> 00:08:44.261
Download the workpaper in Excel.

84
00:08:46.757 --> 00:08:51.267
And it all works in French: one click switches the app, the forms and the downloads.

85
00:09:04.957 --> 00:09:10.432
That's a complete SR&ED claim, federal, Ontario and Quebec, from ledgers and timesheets

86
00:09:10.432 --> 00:09:15.907
to the T661 and every credit form. Thanks so much for watching, and find out more at rdinnovate.com.
